  "summary": "Picks the enemy with the highest current SPEED among enemies within the caster's range (the cast target if none is in range), then for every cell on the straight (supercover) line from the caster to that enemy, each enemy standing on the line takes special damage and has its SPEED lowered; the SPEED is given back after 5000 ms. Allies on the line are untouched.",
  "targeting": {
   "who": "the enemy with the highest speed in range (range from the caster's own stat, Chebyshev distance, centre excluded; no targettable/visibility filter is applied in this function); ties keep the stable sort order of the board scan. The effect then hits EVERY enemy on the line to that enemy, not only that enemy.",
   "needsTarget": true,
   "note": "The line is a supercover line from caster to the chosen enemy, so it can include enemies nearer than the fastest one (and diagonals can touch extra cells). If no enemy is in range the cast target is used instead. The sort uses current speed (after buffs/debuffs at cast time). Enemy scan order within Board.getCellsInRange is row-major (y outer, x inner); the effect of ties on that was derived from the loop, not executed.",
   "evidence": [
